Built stdlib-only compress.py supporting both requested CLI commands, with reversible structured-text preprocessing, compression, and a generic fallback. Verified byte-identical restoration of corpus.txt and five additional edge cases. The registered assay repeatedly reports 98.8989% size reduction: 313,972 bytes become 3,457 bytes, versus 35,399 bytes with default zlib. Scored variants improved substantially over the initial baseline-beating implementation.